\newlabel{app:discovery_results}{{B}{105}{Discovered Nets, Conformance and Rule Audit}{appendix.B}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.1}{\ignorespaces Discovery configurations of E1, all run in ProM Lite 1.4 on the training log (59,139 visits). The iDHM frequency threshold is relative to the number of visits: at 0.1, only directly-follows relations that occur in at least a tenth of the visits are used. Because no data attributes were selected, iDHM discovers no conditional dependencies, and the conditional heuristic (C4.5 with F1 score, condition threshold 0.5) has no effect.}}{106}{table.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:exp_grid}{{B.1}{106}{Discovery configurations of E1, all run in ProM Lite 1.4 on the training log (59,139 visits). The iDHM frequency threshold is relative to the number of visits: at 0.1, only directly-follows relations that occur in at least a tenth of the visits are used. Because no data attributes were selected, iDHM discovers no conditional dependencies, and the conditional heuristic (C4.5 with F1 score, condition threshold 0.5) has no effect}{table.caption.47}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.2}{\ignorespaces Conformance of all discovered nets on the training log (2 March to 11 April 2026) and the test log (13 to 30 April 2026). Fitness, fitting visits and accepted sequences: alignment replay in ProM 6.15 (costs 1 for a move on the log or on a visible transition, 0 for a silent move); fitness is the ProM trace fitness averaged over the visits. Fitting visits: share of visits whose complete sequence the net accepts. Precision: escaping-edges precision, ETConformance in ProM 6.15 on the discovered net, same settings for every net (``Lazy Invisibles'', ``First Indeterminism Solving''). \textsuperscript  {a}\,ETConformance counts 30 training and 15 test visits of IM 0.0 as non-fitting that fit under alignments (Section~\ref {sec:exp_discovery_eval}). Seq.\ accepted: training sequences accepted, of 82. Unseen test seq.: test sequences that do not occur in training and are accepted, of 16. Soundness: WOFLAN (PM4Py implementation). Values of unsound nets are diagnostic only. The prefix tree is a reference that accepts exactly the training sequences.}}{107}{table.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_e1_conformance}{{B.2}{107}{Conformance of all discovered nets on the training log (2 March to 11 April 2026) and the test log (13 to 30 April 2026). Fitness, fitting visits and accepted sequences: alignment replay in ProM 6.15 (costs 1 for a move on the log or on a visible transition, 0 for a silent move); fitness is the ProM trace fitness averaged over the visits. Fitting visits: share of visits whose complete sequence the net accepts. Precision: escaping-edges precision, ETConformance in ProM 6.15 on the discovered net, same settings for every net (``Lazy Invisibles'', ``First Indeterminism Solving''). \textsuperscript {a}\,ETConformance counts 30 training and 15 test visits of IM 0.0 as non-fitting that fit under alignments (Section~\ref {sec:exp_discovery_eval}). Seq.\ accepted: training sequences accepted, of 82. Unseen test seq.: test sequences that do not occur in training and are accepted, of 16. Soundness: WOFLAN (PM4Py implementation). Values of unsound nets are diagnostic only. The prefix tree is a reference that accepts exactly the training sequences}{table.caption.48}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.3}{\ignorespaces Escaping-edges precision of the sound nets of E1 on the training log, by implementation. ProM: ETConformance 6.9.52 with the settings of Section~\ref {sec:exp_discovery_eval}. PM4Py 2.7.22.3: \texttt  {precision\_\allowbreak  token\_\allowbreak  based\_\allowbreak  replay} and \texttt  {precision\_\allowbreak  alignments}. The implementations agree for nets whose silent transitions do not branch; where silent paths branch, PM4Py follows fewer of them and reports a higher value.}}{108}{table.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:app_precision_tools}{{B.3}{108}{Escaping-edges precision of the sound nets of E1 on the training log, by implementation. ProM: ETConformance 6.9.52 with the settings of Section~\ref {sec:exp_discovery_eval}. PM4Py 2.7.22.3: \texttt {precision\_token\_based\_replay} and \texttt {precision\_alignments}. The implementations agree for nets whose silent transitions do not branch; where silent paths branch, PM4Py follows fewer of them and reports a higher value}{table.caption.49}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {B.4}{\ignorespaces Rule audit of the three nets that pass the soundness and coverage checks, as discovered. Rule 3: a visit without a stop is in the language (shortest witness \texttt  {Gate In > Gate Out}). Rule 4: a reachable marking enables two stops at the same time. Rule 5: a mixed stop together with a separate delivery or receive at the same LL or HO2 area is in the language. Bound of rule 6: loops permit any number of stops; the stop guard enforces the planned number in the simulator. A3: rules 3 to 5 hold. Prec.: ETConformance (training).}}{109}{table.caption.50}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rq1_e2_audit}{{B.4}{109}{Rule audit of the three nets that pass the soundness and coverage checks, as discovered. Rule 3: a visit without a stop is in the language (shortest witness \texttt {Gate In > Gate Out}). Rule 4: a reachable marking enables two stops at the same time. Rule 5: a mixed stop together with a separate delivery or receive at the same LL or HO2 area is in the language. Bound of rule 6: loops permit any number of stops; the stop guard enforces the planned number in the simulator. A3: rules 3 to 5 hold. Prec.: ETConformance (training)}{table.caption.50}{}}
